      "pin": false,
      "rows": [
        "entity:Kante direkt (grade 12, 3 stars, 9 C, "Straight up first go.")",
        "entity:Riss (grade 14, 1 stars, 9 C)",
        "entity:Dach (9 C, 70%)",
      ],
      "status": undefined,
      "summary": [
        "3 ascents",
      ],
    },
  ],
  "expected": "One KIND \`session\` card of 3 ascents, and each row carries what THAT climb was logged with: an Opinion strip under Kante direkt holding your own grade and three stars, with your note quoted below it, one under Riss holding your grade and one star, and one under Dach with no Opinion label at all, since an attempt logged with conditions alone said nothing about grade or stars. All three were logged at the same temperature, and the conditions pill sits outside the label on each of them, because a reading is not a take on the climb. The grades are stored as ids here and render through the reader's own scale, the same as the temperature renders through their units, so what the chips say depends on who is looking. The community numbers stay on the rows themselves, which is what the label is there to tell apart. A card-level strip could only ever have shown the first of the three, and did.",
}
`;

